Falsifies `kernel::arch::x86_64::ist::tests::an_nmi_leaves_the_gs_base_it_found`.

Architecture: x86_64

The defect: `isr_paranoid` installs the kernel's GS base and never puts back the one it found, so
an NMI taken in the window between the exit `swapgs` and `iretq` returns to ring 3 with the
kernel's per-CPU address in `IA32_GS_BASE`, and an NMI in the `syscall` entry window leaves
`swapgs` to exchange the wrong pair.

Expected to fail: "the NMI returned with a different GS base from the one it interrupted".
Replayed red on patagonia, 2026-10-13 UTC, `script/test --arch x86_64 --no-host --test an_nmi_leaves_the_gs_base_it_found`
(QEMU q35 under PVH, two cores); green with the fix.

diff --git a/kernel/src/arch/x86_64/trap.s b/kernel/src/arch/x86_64/trap.s
index aefb92483..4c08e72ce 100644
--- a/kernel/src/arch/x86_64/trap.s
+++ b/kernel/src/arch/x86_64/trap.s
@@ -503,7 +503,7 @@ isr_paranoid:
     call x86_paranoid_dispatch
 
     cmp rbx, [rsp + 176]
-    je 2f
+    jmp 2f
     mov ecx, 0xC0000101             # IA32_GS_BASE
     mov rax, rbx
     mov rdx, rbx
